  "goodToKnow": "Währen means to last and is literary or found in proverbs: Was lange währt, wird endlich gut (good things take time), Ehrlich währt am längsten (honesty is the best policy). Everyday German says dauern. The preposition während (during, while) comes from its present participle. Don't confuse it with wahren (to preserve: den Schein wahren) or gewähren (to grant)."
